- model: blawx.ruledoc
  pk: 1
  fields:
    ruledoc_name: Imaginary Alcohol Act (record spelling)
    rule_text: "Imaginary Alcohol Act (record spelling)\n\n1. Imaginary Alcohol Act ss (1)-(2): a body corporate engaging in business for profit, other than a public house or a hotel, must not sell alcohol if it has an unspent conviction for fraud, or an unspent conviction for providing misleading information in relation to an application for a licence under an enactment, or an alcohol banning order.\n2. Imaginary Alcohol Act s (3): where a price list for alcohol is displayed on premises registered as a hotel and the enforcement officer believes the list is misleading to customers, the officer may issue a warning to the proprietor of the premises.\n3. Imaginary Alcohol Act s (4): where a warning has been issued and it is not the case that the proprietor corrected the price list, to the satisfaction of the enforcement officer, within 5 days after the warning was issued, the officer may cancel the registration of the hotel. All three limbs must hold for the proprietor to escape - correcting the list late, or to nobody's satisfaction, leaves the registration cancellable."
    scasp_encoding: ''
    tutorial: ''
    owner: 1
    published: true
- model: blawx.workspace
  pk: 1
  fields:
    ruledoc: 1
    workspace_name: root_section
